{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"bc651fbd5b613366","name":"card_unit_15th_engineers","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/Homefront/units/card_unit_15th_engineers","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"15th ENGINEERS","text":"Deployment: Gain 1 extra kredit slot for each unit in the frontline. Your units gain equal amount of attack.","flavorText":"Formed when the US entered WWI in 1917, the 15th Engineer Battalion began as the 5th Reserve Engineers. After multiple redesignations, it earned battle honors at the Battle of Saint-Mihiel and during the Meuse-Argonne offensive, before being demobilized in 1919. Reactivated in 1940 and assigned to the 9th Infantry Division, it was renamed the 15th Engineer Combat Battalion in 1942 and sent to North Africa. There, it supported operations against the Afrika Korps, then advanced with US forces through Sicily. In June 1944, the battalion landed in Normandy and began clearing mines and building bridges for the 9th Division’s drive across France. It helped enable the first US crossing of the Seine and joined brutal fighting in the Battle of Hürtgen Forest and the Battle of the Bulge. In March 1945, Company B earned a Distinguished Unit Citation for its role in the crossing at Remagen, where the battalion helped secure the Ludendorff Bridge and push deeper into Germany. The unit remained active until late 1946, after having supported every major 9th Division campaign in Europe.","faction":"USA","type":"infantry","rarity":"Rare","cost":5,"operationCost":1,"attack":1,"defense":2},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_15th_engineers","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_15th_engineers_title","SourceString":"15th ENGINEERS","LocalizedString":"15th ENGINEERS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":1,"defense":2,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":5,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_15th_engineers_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Gain 1 extra kredit slot 